					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-28 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3"><strong>FUCK</strong>&nbsp;greg nickels, for real.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp; s</span>omebody tell this bucket-head to regain his focus on downtown gridlock and leave the nightclub management to meinert.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp; a</span>nd if&nbsp;i see construction of one more condo complex, i&rsquo;mma turn this bitch into bellevue and start topplin&rsquo; cranes.</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">every once in a while, the dude gets it right, though.<span>&nbsp; t</span>ake, for example, his recent proclamation of september as &ldquo;<em><strong>Vince&rsquo;s Italian Restaurant Pizzeria Month</strong>;&rdquo; </em>a bold, gutsy, bi-partisan declaration that will undoubtedly stand as his most noteworthy accomplishment of his entire mayoral tenure.<span>&nbsp; g</span>ood on ya, greg!!</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">many of you already be knowin&rsquo; that Vince&rsquo;s is family oriented &ndash; and i&rsquo;m not talkin&rsquo; about the bambino pasta option on the connect-the-dots menu.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp;i</span> mean real family.<span>&nbsp; b</span>lood; thicker than san pellegrino, but slightly thinner (and a few shades darker) than that delicious marinara.</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">Vince Mottola Sr. (pronounced &ldquo;MO-tuh-luh,&rdquo; not &ldquo;mu-TOE-luh,&rdquo; you knuckleheads), founder of your favorite eatin&rsquo; spots in rainier beach, burien, and renton highlands, is wifey&rsquo;s maternal grandfather.<span>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;i</span> had a chance to meet this man on my first-ever visit to seattle in January of &rsquo;97, on the eve of that MONSTER snow storm, at the former queen anne location (currently peso&rsquo;s).&nbsp;<span>&nbsp;i</span> was ushered first-class to &ldquo;the back room&rdquo; and introduced to &ldquo;nono,&rdquo; who graciously extended a hand with three full-length fingers and a couple of nubs, which,&nbsp;i was told later were the result of a &ldquo;cooking accident.&rdquo;<span>&nbsp;&nbsp;i</span> never questioned the explanation, at least not openly, and&nbsp;i never got a chance to see him again before he passed away the following year.</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">Vince came to amurka in &rsquo;54 directly from napoli (naples is in florida, dummy).<span>&nbsp; w</span>ith the skill and knowledge he&rsquo;d gained from working in the catering business back home, he set out to open up a restaurant in the rainier valley &ndash; known at the time as &ldquo;garlic gulch.&rdquo;<span>&nbsp; t</span>he first <em>Vince&rsquo;s </em>opened up in 1957 at othello and empire way, and even though the original spot made way for some snazzy duplexes (whattup, my dude?) they&rsquo;re still holding down the folks around the beach to this day.</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">do the math, genius &ndash; it&rsquo;s FIFTY YEARS of pizza and pasta, and we&rsquo;re callin&rsquo; for a celebration, <strike>bitches</strike>&nbsp;(edit)!<span>&nbsp; c</span>ome out to the restaurant sunday night (8824 renton ave south &ndash; 6pm) and i&rsquo;ll personally deliver your pollo marsalla &ndash; plus i&rsquo;ll introduce you to my &ldquo;nona,&rdquo; who will sing and dance for you, then kiss you on the mouth.<span>&nbsp; i</span>t&rsquo;s a family affair, family!</font></p><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">&nbsp;</font> <p style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt" class="MsoNormal"><font face="Times New Roman" size="3">I&rsquo;ll save a spot for you next to nickels&hellip;<br /><br />RA</font></p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-24 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>Friends,<br /><br />It&rsquo;s <strong>Hari Kondabolu</strong>. Some of you may simply know me as Sabzi&rsquo;s writing partner from the now legendary Massline blog: <strong><a href="http://harithecomic.blogspot.com/2007/08/tour-of-queens-with-blue-scholars.html" target="_blank">The Blue Scholars visit Hari in Queens.</a></strong> <br /><br />For those of you who don&rsquo;t know me (seriously, you don&rsquo;t know me? Where you been???), click here for more information: <strong><a href="http://www.harithecomic.com/bio.htm" target="_blank">WHO IS THIS HARI KONDABOLU?</a></strong><br /><br />Now that formal introductions are out of the way...HELLO FAMILY!<br /><br />Though I left Seattle two months ago to pursue a Masters degree in Human Rights (yes, they make that) at the London School of Economics, I still feel very connected to Seattle and Massline. I believe in what we&rsquo;re doing and I am honored to be an official blogger on this site. In the coming months, I&rsquo;ll give you my thoughts on art, politics, London, music, sports, colonialism&hellip;you know&hellip;stuff<br /><br />Quick <strong>London </strong>update:<br /><br />Chips are called &ldquo;crisps.&rdquo; Cell phones are called &quot;mobiles.&quot; The term &quot;Asian&quot; refers<span class="text"> to South Asians. Americans should call themselves &ldquo;Canadian.&rdquo;</span><br /><br />I&rsquo;m still looking for permanent housing and no one knows who I am here. I need <strong><a href="http://www.myspace.com/harithecomic" target="_blank">more friends</a></strong>.<br /><br />I don&rsquo;t like the air here. I blew my nose the other day and the tissue was filled with soot. No joke. My tissue turned black. The air is that polluted here and it makes me feel terribly unhealthy. Makes me wish I was back in Seattle so the Northwest could fill my lungs, and heal the pain in my chest.  My friend George said something like this. <br /><br />Do ya&#39;ll know George? Filipino dude. Great guy.<span class="text"> Sings for a popular, local rap band some of you might know. </span><span class="text"><br /><br />In closing, here is a </span>clip from my favorite, now defunct, BBC comedy show <strong>Goodness Gracious </strong><strong>Me</strong>. Enjoy!<br /><br /><object width="425" height="350" type="application/x-shockwave-flash" data="http://www.youtube.com/v/bU70qAfQAo8"><br /><param name="movie" value="http://www.youtube.com/v/bU70qAfQAo8"></param></object><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-24 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>more ATL flics:<br /><br />don&#39;t you get it?  if these people like Blue Scholars, you should too.  don&#39;t think for yourself!<br /><strong><br />Hank Shocklee</strong>&nbsp;likes Blue Scholars!<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/shockley.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br /><u><strong><a href="http://www.wishatl.com/">Wish, ATL</a></strong></u> likes Blue Scholars!  (peace Al!)<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/wish2.jpg" alt="" /> <br /><br />now go download the new cut and the upper right. =)<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-24 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><p style="font: normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica; margin: 0px">Big up to the 253&#39;s own <strong>Can-U</strong> on the release of his latest mixtape <strong><em>Hear This</em></strong> (mixed by DJ Reign). My dude dropped the heavily slept-on album <strong><em>A Stepping Stone</em></strong> in 2005 and has been representing the Northwest quietly but consistently since. Mixing some exclusive tracks with tracks from some of his favorite artists (including Blue Scholars &quot;No Rest For the Weary&quot;), Can-U shines with storytelling and wordplay throughout the mix. A solid release as we anticipate the new full-length album (rumored to have a cameo from a <strong>Massline</strong> emcee you might know). On top of all of that, the mixtape is available <strong>FREE</strong> for download on his site, <a href="www.can-u.net">www.can-u.net</a>!</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2007-09-21 | Friday</font></strong><br><br><strong>Atlanta</strong> has been a blast so far.  the digital camera died, so we had to stick to using pictures taken with the <strong>iPhone</strong>.<br /><br />September 20th went as follows:<br /><br />woke up, went to the <strong>Atlantis Music Conference</strong>, dipped outta there, hit up the <strong>New Era Flagship Store</strong> where the <strong>Sneaker Pimps</strong> had a &quot;shoe battle&quot; of some sort (i&#39;m not really sure how that works... do they just NT tap them hella hard?) and then the camera died.  <br /><br />then we hit up <strong>Sol Munki</strong> next door and met up with the dood <strong>Fruit </strong>and started snappin flicks with the phone. <br /><br /><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/munki1.jpg" alt="" /><br /><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/munki2.jpg" alt="" /><br /><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/munki3.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />we only stayed at Sol Munki for a minute, they had a selection of the cre8tive recreation (my personal favorite) and a grip of ill art on the walls.  and hella skateboards. to top it off, they were a selection of the friendliest clothing snobs i&#39;ve met.  my kinda folks.<br /><br />then it was off to <strong>WREK</strong> at <strong>Georgia Tech</strong> to hit up the folks who do <strong>Wrekroom Renaissance</strong> 9pm-11pm every Thursday night.  <strong>A-Dot</strong>, one of the show&#39;s hosts, explained to us that WREK has had hip hop on that time slot since &#39;86 and their show has been carrying the tradition.  wowsers.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/wrek1.jpg" alt="" /><br /><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/wrek2.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />the show went well.  we talked music, business, avoided cursing and ticket prices, and gave praise to the man with the illest DJ name of the week: <strong>DJ Black Daniels</strong>.  this dood by the name of <strong>Jaz-O</strong> then walked in as we were on our way out and our foolish selves didn&#39;t get a photo. =(<br /><br />on the way back to the hotel, i saw this:<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/dna.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />kind of a weird bumper sticker to put at a freeway exit...<br /><br />next, after a long cab ride that included getting lost and finding that all the streets in ATL are named &quot;Peachtree,&quot; we hit up the <strong>Remix Hotel</strong> producer/beatmaker battle at the Hard Rock Cafe.  we missed the battle (damn Peachtrees!) but got a chance to see <strong>Talib</strong> rock the stage.  it was filthy.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/kiashine.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />outside the club, i got a chance to get krispy with my kinfolk <strong>Kia Shine</strong>.  apparently, the man is very tall and has lots of love for Seattle.  that&#39;s my guy.  &quot;Stunna Frames&quot; was on my myspace page for like 5 months straight.  gee, i look sleepy and high in that picture.<br /><br /> <img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/talib.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />then we had a chance to <strong>get by</strong> in the lobby of the Westin.<br /><br />i have a friend that works at this club called <strong>Compound</strong> where, apparently, they make it rain.  for real.  Three 6 Mafia and Jeezy were supposed to be there that night and i was trying to see some $100 bills falling from the sky.  unfortunately, nobody wanted to go.<br /> <br />so, after another overpriced cab ride and dodging about 37 strip clubs, we made it back to the hotel to watch <strong>Nice &amp; Smooth</strong> rock the end of an <strong>In Living Color</strong> rerun.<br /><br /><img src="http://www.masslinemedia.com/images/ATL1/nice.jpg" alt="" /><br /><br />we&#39;ll see what happens tomorrow.<br /><br />saba<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> [16] <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?f